nity establish any  particular rules or way of doing things  we can play it safe by saying that the  shadily order practiced the most  universal sufi ritual known as thikr or  remembrance where names of god or the  muslim proclamation of faith is repeated  for long periods of time one will often  have regular gatherings called hadra in  which practices like these are performed  and as with all other orders the  shadolis have their own weird or prayers  and prayer cycles that are given to  initiates by their sheikh and which are  recited either privately and in or in  group  allah in fact did write a treatise  dedicated to vikkit in particular called  miftah falah the key to salvation in  which he defends the practice as well as  its vocal performance in particular so  that is the  vocal chanting of vikkan that is perhaps  the most common in sufism where people  will sit in groups and will they will  chant vocally sometimes pretty loudly  the names of god or the proclamation of  faith some  other muslims and even sufi muslims were  against this idea of doing it vocally  but most weren't and ibna ta'ala writes  this treatise  where he among other things defends this  uh vocal practice of thicker so we know  that the shadows even in the early  periods did perform thicker and that  they did so vocally but other than these  basic practices there is really not much  that characterizes the chadelia in  particular  and because it has spread so widely  across north africa as well as the rest  of the world we see a lot of variety and  diversity between regions and branches  of the order so it's difficult to say  something in particular  that characterizes the order in general  just as in many other sufi traditions  the shadolist view as important the  visiting or ziara to the shrine of  ashadhi where he is buried which is in  humaith egypt as i mentioned and they  will often gather there annually usually  on his birthday or maulid going to this  one village in in egypt and th