ovement that has emerged in  the last century that emphasizes a  perennial wisdom that hides within all  of the world's quote-unquote true  religions often with the view that sufi  oriented islam is the most complete  expression of this perennial wisdom the  representatives of this school are often  followers of ahmed al-alawi in  particular who kind of created a branch  of his own within the shadolia darqawiya  which is often called the chavelia  alawia now these branches and super  branches often get very complicated and  complex but stay with me here in a case  this perennial school often associated  with the shadily order in particular has  been represented by figures like the  already mentioned rene guenon fritschev  shuwon martin lynx and the current most  prominent teacher and philosopher syed  jose nasser  this group of scholars have also been  instrumental in bringing the work of  many sufi scholars of history to a  western audience such as many  translations and interpretations of  figures like ibn arabi and mulasadra and  they do shape our understanding of these  figures to a massive degree but not all  prominent shadily figures in the west  are connected to the traditionalist  school or the alawia the american  islamic scholar no hameem keller is also  an adherent of the shadoli darqawi order  and is often considered one of the most  important muslim teachers in the world  today through his many publications and  commitment to online education we should  also mention the recently passed  american sufi nourodin durki may he rest  in peace who further spread the order to  the u.s and very interestingly also has  connections to other contemporary  figures like ramdas and was actually  largely responsible in his youth for the  publication of his very popular work  called be here now  it is because of the popularity of the  shadolia among scholars and western  converts of high intellectual status  that the shadowy order has become famous  as an order that in 